{
  "id": "geo-foundations",
  "chapterNumber": "1",
  "title": {
    "en": "Foundations &amp; Reasoning",
    "ar": null
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Geometry begins with undefined terms — point, line, plane — and builds outward through definitions and logical argument. Most early results come from a handful of angle relationships.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 1.1 — Angle pairs",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Two angles are <strong>complementary</strong> if they sum to \\( 90^{\\circ} \\) and <strong>supplementary</strong> if they sum to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\). A <strong>linear pair</strong> (adjacent angles on a straight line) is always supplementary, and <strong>vertical angles</strong> (opposite at an intersection) are always equal.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Midpoint",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( M=\\Big(\\tfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\tfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\Big) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Complementary",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\alpha+\\beta=90^{\\circ} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Supplementary",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\alpha+\\beta=180^{\\circ} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Vertical angles",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "equal in measure",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the complement of \\( 35^{\\circ} \\).</p>\\[ 90^{\\circ}-35^{\\circ}=55^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Angles \\( \\angle 1 \\) and \\( \\angle 2 \\) form a linear pair with \\( \\angle 1=125^{\\circ} \\). Find \\( \\angle 2 \\).</p>\\[ 180^{\\circ}-125^{\\circ}=55^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
